AFFIDAVIT

I, Dr. Anil Kumar Sharma, S/o Late Shri Rameshwar Sharma, aged 55 years,
residing at 15, Sushant Lok, Gurgaon – 122 009,
Electrical Engineering Consultant,
do hereby solemnly affirm and state as follows:

1. I am a qualified Electrical Engineer with 30 years of experience in power sector projects
   and have been engaged as a consultant by M/s. Power Grid Infra Projects Pvt. Ltd. for the
   220 kV GIS Substation Project.

2. I have personally inspected the construction site on multiple occasions and have
   reviewed all technical drawings, equipment specifications, and quality compliance records.

3. Regarding the 220 kV GIS equipment supply delay: The GIS equipment is critical for
   substation operation. Without this equipment, the following works cannot be completed:
   - GIS room civil works (equipment dimensions required)
   - Control room cabling and panel installation
   - Protection system testing and commissioning
   - Grid synchronization and energization

4. The contract Clause 15 clearly stipulates that RVPNL shall supply the GIS equipment
   within 6 months of site handover. The delay of 282 days is a clear breach of this obligation.

5. Regarding the additional bay (VO-01): The additional 220 kV bay was indeed instructed
   by RVPNL for future load enhancement. This is a valid variation and should be compensated
   as per RVPNL GCC Clause 12.

6. The rate analysis prepared by my office shows that the fair compensation for the
   additional bay work is ₹1.82 Crore.

7. Regarding quality of work: I have personally inspected all civil works, electrical
   installations, and tower foundations. The quality is fully compliant with:
   - IS 2026:2018 (220 kV GIS Substation Equipment)
   - IEEE 1547:2018 (Interconnection Standards)
   - IEEMA specifications for electrical equipment
   - CPWD specifications for civil works

8. Test certificates for all electrical equipment show 100% compliance with
   target specifications. No technical deficiencies have been identified.

9. Regarding the Transmission Line RoW: Land acquisition for transmission line RoW is
   the statutory responsibility of the state government through RVPNL. The 120-day delay
   in RoW handover is beyond the contractor's control.

10. Regarding price escalation: Copper prices increased by 65%, steel by 58%, and electrical
    equipment by 42% since base date May 2024. This escalation is well beyond the threshold
    and should be compensated as per IEEMA Price Variation Clause.

11. All facts stated above are within my professional knowledge and are true to the best of my
    information and belief. No part of it is false and nothing material has been concealed.

Deponent: Dr. Anil Kumar Sharma
Date: 01.12.2025
Place: Gurgaon

Sworn before me:
Oath Commissioner / Notary Public